{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for","id":386678,"title":"Solars, what foreign magic are you most excited for?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-30T14:33:03-08:00","id":386678,"title":"Solars, what foreign magic are you most excited for?","content":"One of the unique things about the Solar Exalted is the ability to take the commonly available sources of external magical power (Sorcery, Martial Arts, Evocations) and take them up to the highest level possible. With 3E coming around the corner, what are you going to bee-line towards with your first character? This is, of course, assuming your ST doesn't just drown you in XP and you have to be choosy.<br /> <br /> Personally, I am most excited about the new Sorcery system. Sorcery in Exalted is how I always wanted a magic system to be, but could never find it: Slow but extraordinarily powerful, a strategic resource as well as a tactical weapon or tool, and what makes me even more excited is the concept of Sorcerous workings that let me place powerful, potentially permanent spells on places, people or things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 01-30-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:45:03-08:00","id":386704,"title":"","content":"Evocations. I really like this idea that our artifacts are now legendary and interesting and <i>unique</i> in their own right.<br /> <br /> I am so looking forward to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:45:40-08:00","id":386706,"title":"","content":"For me...Sorcery and Evocations. I have a Twilight concept in mind: a big burly Lookshyan smith/engineer who is primarily going to be using Solar Brawl as his combat ability, so MA is not at the top of my priority list (though at some far-off point, his interest in natural Essence patterns is going to push him towards Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style). He's likely going to start as a sorcerer, having been trained in certain applications of the art in his mortal life, and I want to play with Evocations he'd unlock on his smashfists. <br /> <br /> I've thought of him being the sort of person to be riding a Cloud Trapeze above the battlefield as his Circle engages a foe, relaying strategic information to them before casting Invulnerable Skin of Bronze or Incomparable Body Arsenal and swan-diving from a great height into the fray. <br /> <br /> Part of my relative disinterest in MA is this concept, and part is due to the brand-newness of Evocations and the total Sorcery execution revamp (I guess I don't think MA will be paradigmatically changing as much as Sorcery is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:49:10-08:00","id":386709,"title":"","content":"Evocations, finally my 'legendary weapon' is going to feel like it is worthy of being called that instead of just being a big chunk of unbreakable metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:59:27-08:00","id":386722,"title":"","content":"I'm personally excited about all of them, although I'm probably going to pick which one or two I go with based on what my first character's concept is.<br /> <br /> Since it would be my first time playing a tabletop rpg instead of a crpg (unless I play something else between then and now), I'll probably be making a good ol' fighty-man, and thus I'd go with Martial Arts and/or Evocations. But you never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:15:20-08:00","id":386727,"title":"","content":"Sorcery and Martial Arts are the big headlines for me. Once the book drops I want to try making a homebrewed MA style and related Occult Charms to tie the two concepts together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:33:35-08:00","id":386740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=386706#post386706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've thought of him being the sort of person to be riding a Cloud Trapeze above the battlefield as his Circle engages a foe, relaying strategic information to them before casting Invulnerable Skin of Bronze or Incomparable Body Arsenal and swan-diving from a great height into the fray.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:46:13-08:00","id":386755,"title":"","content":"Sorcery and Evocations. I've got a Southeastern Twilight Caste planned as a major Sorcerer (she's from the area nearbyish Rathess), and I've got a... well, technically it's an Abyssal with an eye for redemption as a major part of her story arc, but she'll use Evocations off the Dire Lance that her Past Life used.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've <i>also</i> got a Zenith Caste who uses Crane Style (actually, she's my avatar pic), but her Martial Arts is focused on Crane Style mostly because it has a lot of capacity for non-lethal combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","user":"horngeek","date":". 01-30-2015, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:50:44-08:00","id":386760,"title":"","content":"Evocations for sure, and if it's true that all martial arts styles are good for Solars without feeling like I'm wasting my time with them, then those too. I get to be a Solar as well as raising up earth walls with my white jade goremaul and burn bitches with my fire breath? Fuck the hell yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T16:02:28-08:00","id":386791,"title":"","content":"Sorcery, performing those epic workings of magic such that each will become a legend of its own. Also, crafting; now that wonders are real, and making them will involve more than just churning out Big Sword +5 at discount prices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T17:18:15-08:00","id":386861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=386706#post386706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought of him being the sort of person to be riding a Cloud Trapeze above the battlefield as his Circle engages a foe, relaying strategic information to them before casting Invulnerable Skin of Bronze or Incomparable Body Arsenal and swan-diving from a great height into the fray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of the stunt my Dawn Caste did when elbow-dropping onto a bandit from on high.<br /> <br /> Namely, said stunt described the bandit opening a fortune cookie after his lunch, to read &quot;Look to the skies to realize your destiny,&quot; only to realize he was standing in shadow all of a sudden...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:03:21-08:00","id":387492,"title":"","content":"I always wanted to take Sorcery and couldn't justify the expense, so I'm looking forward to that, but I think I'm most curious about Evocations just because they're totally new, and the niche they fill (a way to make artifacts live up to their hype without being overpowered or inaccessible) was badly needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:18:32-08:00","id":387497,"title":"","content":"You know, sorcery plus evocations makes a western style Wizard with powerful magic and badass magic staff super easy to me. Not likely one of the design goals, but I have a few players with a strong D&amp;D background that would appreciate it a lot.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not super excited about any of the foreign magics. All of them kinda lost their novelty to me a long time ago. I'll have to wait for Sids to get my Sidereal Martial Arts fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:24:11-08:00","id":387501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387497#post387497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, sorcery plus evocations makes a western style Wizard with powerful magic and badass magic staff super easy to me. Not likely one of the design goals, but I have a few players with a strong D&amp;D background that would appreciate it a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>If doing this is exalted is wrong, I do not want to be right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Oe7Q8OCm5I </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387497#post387497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not super excited about any of the foreign magics. All of them kinda lost their novelty to me a long time ago. I'll have to wait for Sids to get my Sidereal Martial Arts fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even evocations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:26:44-08:00","id":387503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=386861#post386861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of the stunt my Dawn Caste did when elbow-dropping onto a bandit from on high.<br /> <br /> Namely, said stunt described the bandit opening a fortune cookie after his lunch, to read &quot;Look to the skies to realize your destiny,&quot; only to realize he was standing in shadow all of a sudden...</div> </div> </div> </div>*warning, graphic as hell*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sFYEicpJfFM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sFYEicpJfFM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sFYEicpJfFM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sFYEicpJfFM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:28:32-08:00","id":387504,"title":"","content":"Evocations, so I can itch that shonen anime itch.<br /> <br /> Or Sorcery so I can bind and entreat with demons and princes, lengthen my life by eating ground bones, divide a soul into passive and active halves sealing both in vessels of flesh, curse a queen to be barren and her lands follow suit, quicken a freshly dead person into service so it may yet beget a child, work terrible power upon my foes and the world, anything straight out of the Flat Earth series","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 01-31-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:45:01-08:00","id":387532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387501#post387501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been one to invest heavily in my equipment. It's an interesting concept, but doesn't really excited me. I don't want my power coming from my sword I want it coming from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T12:45:01-08:00","id":387555,"title":"","content":"Sorcery and Evocations are definitely big interests of mine. Also really interested to see what's up with the Crafting system. In the end though, playing a Solar in a game that's not broken will definitely be the highlight!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T12:47:40-08:00","id":387559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387532#post387532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been one to invest heavily in my equipment. It's an interesting concept, but doesn't really excited me. I don't want my power coming from my sword I want it coming from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean technically it's coming from your soul resonating with the spirit of your weapon.<br /> <br /> I think it was said that 2 Solars picking up the same daiklave may not ever call forth the same Evocations from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T13:04:04-08:00","id":387583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387559#post387559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean technically it's coming from your soul resonating with the spirit of your weapon.<br /> <br /> I think it was said that 2 Solars picking up the same daiklave may not ever call forth the same Evocations from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, that's kinda the problem. You need <i>that</i> daiklave, in particular, otherwise you're hosed. I can't speak for Hark, but I personally dislike investing heavily in something that can be easily lost through in-game shenanigans. Yeah you can pick up things like Summoning the Loyal Steel, but that's putting even more eggs into the one basket.<br /> <br /> Also, as Godjaw mentions, it invokes shonen, which outside a few particular series I don't like all that much. I put a lot of the blame on <i>Bleach</i>, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T13:06:33-08:00","id":387584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387583#post387583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, that's kinda the problem. You need <i>that</i> daiklave, in particular, otherwise you're hosed. I can't speak for Hark, but I personally dislike investing heavily in something that can be easily lost through in-game shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctity of Merits is a Thing, dude.<br /> <br /> Also if your Artifacts are easily lost I am comfortable suggesting you're not playing very smart, or have a dick GM. And no mechanics can stop a dick GM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387583#post387583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah you can pick up things like Summoning the Loyal Steel, but that's putting even more eggs into the one basket.</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking up a couple Charms to always have your magic sword available is logical not over investment lol I cannot take this &quot;criticism&quot; seriously at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T14:15:21-08:00","id":387612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387584#post387584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picking up a couple Charms to always have your magic sword available is logical not over investment lol I cannot take this &quot;criticism&quot; seriously at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's keep things civil, hm?<br /> <br /> As for my answer, mostly Sorcery, but I have to admit I wouldn't mind a staff with some Evocations to go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T14:22:12-08:00","id":387613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387584#post387584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctity of Merits is a Thing, dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you want to roll. I personally have never been in a group that felt that...is it on your character sheet? Then it's fair game.<br /> <br /> To put it in context, if your opponent has all his mojo wrapped up in Frostmourne, than it's stupid of you to not to try and deprive him of his magic pokey stick. Whether Froustmourne's owner is a PC or NPC doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> Sauren: Bullshit! Those fucking hobbits can't destroy my ring, I payed for it with Artifact dots <i>and</i> XP!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T14:38:41-08:00","id":387615,"title":"","content":"A spear and shield martial art would make me happy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387583#post387583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, that's kinda the problem. You need <i>that</i> daiklave, in particular, otherwise you're hosed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that someone who's put XP into their spear's evocations has also put XP into the melee ability and melee charms. The evocations simply let them do things with their spear that regular solar charms can't accomplish at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 01-31-2015, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T14:41:59-08:00","id":387619,"title":"","content":"I do love me some Kung Fu and all, but the new sorcery system is what rows my boat. Evocations are gonna be a great addition to the game as well and what i was very hype on for a long while but the sheer creativity in Sorcerous Workings blows my mind. My first character is without any doubt going to pay somebody to teach her sorcery shortly after her Exaltation which will happen in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:00:45-08:00","id":387662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387613#post387613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's how you want to roll. I personally have never been in a group that felt that...is it on your character sheet? Then it's fair game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you play then I have no idea how StLS is not the obvious solution. 8 XP and you're pretty well set to make &quot;my weapon is stolen&quot; a pretty trivial problem to solve.<br /> <br /> I hope that 3e makes Sanctity of Merits as big of a Thing as NWoD did. As in, okay, somehow the sword you invested 200 XP worth of Evocations into is irrevocably destroyed (aka a thing that can't really ever happen if you only buy MA/Sorcery/native Charms). I'd hope you get a refund, because otherwise you seriously devalue Evocations with that kind of risk attached to their investment...and how is that fun? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387613#post387613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it in context, if your opponent has all his mojo wrapped up in Frostmourne, than it's stupid of you to not to try and deprive him of his magic pokey stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first, all your mojo is likely not to be wrapped up in one thing, unless you're investing all your normal and Solar XP into your Evocations. And if you are, but aren't taking precautions to not have your super-mojo shit stolen...that's basically your stupid decision coming home to roost. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387613#post387613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether Froustmourne's owner is a PC or NPC doesn't really matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it does. You chose to play a guy who expresses super puissance through his weapon. If your ST is constantly trying to deprive you of your weapon, and makes a sad face because he can't steal another character's Sorcery or Martial Arts, then they're seriously a dick. Explain to me how it's fun to constantly try to deprive a player of their concept, versus that being a point in one story arc (versus a tactic in every story arc). Every single Thundercats arc didn't revolve around stealing the Sword of Omens, for example. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387613#post387613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sauren: Bullshit! Those fucking hobbits can't destroy my ring, I payed for it with Artifact dots <i>and</i> XP!</div> </div> </div> </div>You gotta be kidding. Examples like this, which draw from purely narrative non-game sources, are complete strawman. Not to mention absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:19:02-08:00","id":387671,"title":"","content":"Evocations leave me cold so far.<br /> <br /> I am super excited about the sheer number of Martial Arts styles in the core; though there are a few I am missing. I am definitely looking forward to build some Martial Artists.<br /> <br /> Sorcery... my interest has come and gone and come again over the years. I like the idea, but not so much the 1e and 2e implementations. And I mostly gravitate towards Sorcery with Lunars and Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:38:46-08:00","id":387702,"title":"","content":"even being a sorcery fan, what i'm more excited is about evocations, i really want to have my objects be able to unleash a bankai <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:42:29-08:00","id":387720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope that 3e makes Sanctity of Merits as big of a Thing as NWoD did. As in, okay, somehow the sword you invested 200 XP worth of Evocations into is irrevocably destroyed (aka a thing that can't really ever happen if you only buy MA/Sorcery/native Charms). I'd hope you get a refund, because otherwise you seriously devalue Evocations with that kind of risk attached to their investment...and how is that fun? </div> </div> </div>John seems to share your sentiment that it would be bad to have people lose all that XP they paid for evocations if they are permanently deprived of the artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh yeah, there are definitely time and scope issues that I am still addressing behind the scenes. But let's say you got a daiklave out of a ruin and it got destroyed? You won't be out whatever theoretical experience you put into it. Even if that means I write a clause in the rules saying you get your experience points back. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:00:58-08:00","id":387726,"title":"","content":"Eclipse-Okay Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:16:39-08:00","id":387756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387662#post387662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's how you play then I have no idea how StLS is not the obvious solution. 8 XP and you're pretty well set to make &quot;my weapon is stolen&quot; a pretty trivial problem to solve.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, &quot;Spend motes and solve plots&quot; Charms are terrible game design. I'm hoping that they stuck to their guns and eliminted as many of those as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope that 3e makes Sanctity of Merits as big of a Thing as NWoD did. As in, okay, somehow the sword you invested 200 XP worth of Evocations into is irrevocably destroyed (aka a thing that can't really ever happen if you only buy MA/Sorcery/native Charms). I'd hope you get a refund, because otherwise you seriously devalue Evocations with that kind of risk attached to their investment...and how is that fun? </div> </div> </div>If I could answer your question with a question: how is a game fun <i>without</i> risk and challenge? You put Artifact dots and Charms into your daiklave? That's fine, but you're taking the risk that it'll get nicked or destroyed. Unless Evocations are stupidly overpowerdly broken, I don't see the risk:reward of them panning out.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a player takes Tiger Warrior Training, is it then not okay for an adversary to attack their troops? They invested time and a Charm into getting those troops. If they have farmland or trade caravans, can the antagonist not burn or pillage them? Why is it okay to attack one aspect of an enemy's infrastructure, but not another?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Explain to me how it's fun to constantly try to deprive a player of their concept, versus that being a point in one story arc (versus a tactic in every story arc). Every single Thundercats arc didn't revolve around stealing the Sword of Omens, for example. </div> </div> </div>But if the enemy in question has the time, resources, motivation and temperant to steal the Sword of Omens, why should they not? It's a legit attack vector. Your monster of the week shouldn't be going after the Sword of Omens, but Mum-Ra sure as hell should be...Lion-o without the Sword is much less of a threat than Lion-o with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You gotta be kidding. Examples like this, which draw from purely narrative non-game sources, are complete strawman. Not to mention absurd. </div> </div> </div>Cos it's absurd. Why d'ya think I wrote it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387615#post387615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that someone who's put XP into their spear's evocations has also put XP into the melee ability and melee charms. The evocations simply let them do things with their spear that regular solar charms can't accomplish at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so do I. I'm just saying I feel that Evocations are comparatively risky investment. I don't know if I would say <i>bad</i> investment just yet. Playing equipment dependent characters in the past has taught me that, if at all possible, you should never have any piece or set of equipment that's so precious as to be irreplacable, because the general chaos of the game <i>will</i> practically ensure you'll be without them at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:24:36-08:00","id":387760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I could answer your question with a question: how is a game fun <i>without</i> risk and challenge? You put Artifact dots and Charms into your daiklave? That's fine, but you're taking the risk that it'll get nicked or destroyed. Unless Evocations are stupidly overpowerdly broken, I don't see the risk:reward of them panning out.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a player takes Tiger Warrior Training, is it then not okay for an adversary to attack their troops? They invested time and a Charm into getting those troops. If they have farmland or trade caravans, can the antagonist not burn or pillage them? Why is it okay to attack one aspect of an enemy's infrastructure, but not another? </div> </div> </div>You didn't pay XP for the tiger warriors (probably, unless your ST makes you pay XP for things you earn through in story actions), you paid XP to gain the ability to make tiger warriors and can continue to train more if some of them get destroyed. A more accurate analogy would be if your ST declared that your opponent had somehow made it so that you are incapable of training new tiger warriors and that charm you spent XP on is useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:41:59-08:00","id":387780,"title":"","content":"I'm like... Soooooo torn.<br /> I think I'll enjoy them all, and there's a fair chance that I'll use all three of them in my first 3E character. Because it really isn't all that ridiculous to have, say, an Eclipse-caste pirate captain that conjures sorcerous winds to carry her ship against the currents, and who is using a sword-based martial art with her Blue Jade Wavecleaver Crying Monsoon - a perfectly &quot;normal&quot; concept for Exalted, yet it would reasonably use all three avenues.<br /> <br /> That being said, probably Sorcery. Because I expect that MA will not change that much, you know, I expect it <i>to work</i>, but it'll probably still make my character do the same shit it was supposed to do in 1 &amp; 2E - and in my rounds, we have house ruled Evocations for ages now, I think ever since we stole the idea of leveling your artifact from Dark Age of Camelot, the MMO, so really, Sorcerous Workings are the thing that seems most new to me, and the examples that have been hinted it, of what it might do, look super interesting to me.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to undertake crazy projects. Crazy magic projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:47:19-08:00","id":387785,"title":"","content":"One of the things I like in Exalted is the idea of you being the bearer of your own power. In 2e, Charms were everything. This was problematic in many ways, but I did think it was cool. On the flip side, items and equipment has never really interested me. Evocations might change that, but it's something that 3e will have to convince me of, not something I'm looking forward to in particular.<br /> <br /> What I look forward to are the Charms and Martial Arts. I expect great things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:51:00-08:00","id":387791,"title":"","content":"Given comments about how having Allies as a Merit doesn't insulate them from being killed, I have my doubts about sanctity of Merits. I would find the occasion where your Allies being killed provides you with XP in any context besides roleplaying your response to be pretty weird, and that's not even covering the idea of hundreds of XP. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying I feel that Evocations are comparatively risky investment. I don't know if I would say bad investment just yet. Playing equipment dependent characters in the past has taught me that, if at all possible, you should never have any piece or set of equipment that's so precious as to be irreplacable, because the general chaos of the game will practically ensure you'll be without them at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the power to incinerate cities might be worth the risks, that the indestructibility of Artifacts makes the risk of the thing being broken in about the same area as the risk of one's character dying, if not even harder, and that having the Artifact stolen can be a suitable plot development for efforts to get it back, so long as the ST is not frustrating and arbitrary about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T17:29:31-08:00","id":387849,"title":"","content":"I freely admit a childish fondness for big, impressive, flashy things, which regrettably puts Martial Arts as a distant third out of the Evocations-Sorcery-MA group. Not that there aren't flashy things to be found in Martial Arts, but -- outside SMAs and the more unusual styles -- it's not what comes quickest to mind. Still cool, and I can see some characters of mine digging it, but they're definitely not where I expect I'll be gravitating. Though who knows! There are some neat styles in the Core, and Vance's write-ups may well knock my socks off.<br /> <br /> Evocations are probably a close second of the three. Like Weimann above, I'm usually not that keen on items and equipment in RPGs. With Evocations, though, I dunno. Something about the way they've been described has my interest and I can see a lot of potential there. The idea that multiple bearers of a given artifact can each draw different sets of Evocations from it really sells me on the idea that it <i>is</i> about a personal connection the character has forged with the artifact, not just a bunch of powers. I dig it, and it makes me want to create a character where the artifact and its Evocations do make up a good swath of his capabilities.<br /> <br /> Sorcery's topping the list at the moment, and just about everyone who's mentioned it has already iterated why. I really, really want to see the initiation paths, as they're probably what's most recently captivated me; some of the teasers Vance has dropped really have my interest. And that's on top of sorcerous workings sounding just ridiculously flush with possibilities, and spells sounding less suicidal in most forms of combat. The idea of different mote-gathering methods for shaping spells also sounds like it could add some tactical depth and incentives to play in certain interesting ways. So, MA and Evocations are cool, but they just don't feel like they can compete with Sorcery. We'll see how things shape out in the end, but it's gonna be exciting. ^_^<br /> <br /> Ah. And Eclipse-Only Charms also sound neat. Just... &gt;.&gt; Not sure where to put them. Maybe a bit spiffier than Martial Arts...? I dunno. Looking forward to them, too, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T17:35:24-08:00","id":387879,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have a problem with evocations, they just don't get me excited. The same with Martial Arts, and Sorcery. I expect my players to simply eat up evocations. One has a Sword that have practically been begging for evocations since the character was first made back in probably 2007 maybe earlier. Another almost started salivating what I told him about evocations. He wants to develop defensive evocations for his Super Heavy Plate, the tougher he can get the better, and he will run out of resistance charms eventually.<br /> <br /> Me personally, I might actually end up making that Sorcery/Evocation using wizard with little to no charm usage, not because sorcery and evocation are interesting, but because it makes a personally weak character mastering outside forces for his power. It's the weakness that makes the character interesting, not the magic and artifacts of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T20:37:09-08:00","id":387945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the enemy in question has the time, resources, motivation and temperant to steal the Sword of Omens, why should they not? It's a legit attack vector. Your monster of the week shouldn't be going after the Sword of Omens, but Mum-Ra sure as hell should be...Lion-o without the Sword is much less of a threat than Lion-o with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When one of Mum-Ra's many plans to steal the Sword of Omens actually succeeds, the chronicle then enters a story arc where Lion-o learns the important lesson that he doesn't need to rely on his artifact and is still pretty awesome without it... then he recovers it just in time to use it to save the show.<br /> <br /> Hasn't Saturday morning cartoons taught you anything?<br /> <br /> So, yes, when you invest experience into drawing out the power of an artifact, you <i>do</i> risk loosing access to that investment, <b><i>but</i> </b>it should not be routinely and never permanently -- which could either means recovery, replacement, or reimbursement as the story progresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:53:50-08:00","id":388088,"title":"","content":"The arc of taking the artifact away - or even breaking it in a suitable epic moment despite it being unbreakable (hello, Excalibur-the-awesome-movie!) - is a great thing to do, just not a thing to overuse. Much like placing a loved one in danger, inciting riots in the country the PCs are influent in, having a bad guy take over their organization, and several other such plots. But it comes with the understanding such things do not happen at RANDOM. There is a rhyme and reason to mess with things-that-have-a-dot-cost. You expect it to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 02-01-2015, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T00:37:52-08:00","id":388110,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts because it's always been a little wonky in the first two editions. If the team pulls off supernatural kung fu that has enticing elements for most Exalted types as well as make Sidereal MA work well I am beyond sold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T00:49:43-08:00","id":388120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388110#post388110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts because it's always been a little wonky in the first two editions. If the team pulls off supernatural kung fu that has enticing elements for most Exalted types as well as make Sidereal MA work well I am beyond sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial arts are more interesting to me on other splats then they are on solars for some reason, possibly because there are more splats that can access SMA then their are that can access top tier evocations and top tier sorcery (from what we know only solars get top tier evocations and if it follows 2E then the only other exalt type with access to 3rd circle sorcery will be infernals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T01:15:48-08:00","id":388129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388120#post388120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts are more interesting to me on other splats then they are on solars for some reason, possibly because there are more splats that can access SMA then their are that can access top tier evocations and top tier sorcery (from what we know only solars get top tier evocations and if it follows 2E then the only other exalt type with access to 3rd circle sorcery will be infernals).</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Evocations, we don't actually know that. We know that Solars are the undisputed masters at Evocations, and can get all three levels of Evocations for all magical materials. Other splats not being as good with them can mean a number of different things. It's certainly plausible that some of them might wrangle adamant-level Evocations from particular magical materials. I also recall some mention (ages ago, granted) that Dragonblooded had &quot;a special dispensation&quot; where Evocations were concerned. Time will tell if anything comes of that!<br /> <br /> Regarding Sorcery, I agree in broad strokes, but recall that Sorcery's getting heavily restructured. My vaguely educated guess at this point is that Solar Sorcerers can access the third circle from any &quot;initiation path,&quot; while Abyssal Sorcerers of the 3rd circle may be limited to the Necromancy &quot;path,&quot; and Infernals of the 3rd circle may be able to get them in any, but have a good chance of being similarly limited to one particular (likely Yozi-tied?) &quot;path.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T01:28:09-08:00","id":388131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might actually end up making that Sorcery/Evocation using wizard with little to no charm usage, not because sorcery and evocation are interesting, but because it makes a personally weak character mastering outside forces for his power. It's the weakness that makes the character interesting, not the magic and artifacts of power.</div> </div> </div> </div> That might kind of work for sorcery, but it seems really unfeasable for Evocations. You don't comprehensively master the power of a weapon by being no good at fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T01:36:08-08:00","id":388133,"title":"","content":"Unless something has changed, we totally know that. When they gave us an artifacts evocation tree a sizeable chunk of it was locked behind a solar charm (call the blade) as a prerequisite to learning them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/804449\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...n/posts/804449</a><br /> <br /> I count 7 evocations in the cascade that starts with call the blade. So even assuming that, hypothetically speaking, another type of exalt could learn 3rd tier evocations they still won't be as good with it as a solar.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:19:03-08:00","id":388175,"title":"","content":"I vaguely remember dev-posts stating that evocations are actually &quot;better&quot; than just &quot;plain&quot; native charms, with the weakness that you could loose access to them, the same way an unarmed fighter was weaker than an equally specialised armed fighter, but with the advantage that the unarmed fighter couldn't loose his weapons. <br /> <br /> So, if I remember that correctly, &quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot; is only a thing in so far that the devs plan to make sure that if you loose them, you get something else in return (at the very least, XP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:23:40-08:00","id":388176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388175#post388175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember dev-posts stating that evocations are actually &quot;better&quot; than just &quot;plain&quot; native charms, with the weakness that you could loose access to them, the same way an unarmed fighter was weaker than an equally specialised armed fighter, but with the advantage that the unarmed fighter couldn't loose his weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the other way around, here a quote by John from the Ask the Dev thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Solar with nothing but bare fists and Brawl Charms would trounce a Solar using a daiklave and nothing but Evocations. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-01-2015, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:31:29-08:00","id":388181,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it's because I've spent months hip-deep in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> material, but I really want to go hog-wild with Evocations when I get to play in a proper game rather than a playtest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:53:15-08:00","id":388189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388181#post388181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it's because I've spent months hip-deep in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> material, but I really want to go hog-wild with Evocations when I get to play in a proper game rather than a playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect a lot of people will, since they are the awesome new thing of the edition and will get their support book near instantly while the martial arts and sorcery supplements won't be out for awhile (granted, the Core is going to be crammed full of something like 12 martial arts styles and We got an expanded amount of sorcery from kickstarter as well.)<br /> <br /> How close would you say Arms is to being finished? Still in the repeatedly rewrite to correct flaws that come up in play testing phase? Or maybe close to your final draft you can send in for editing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:10:45-08:00","id":388234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388181#post388181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it's because I've spent months hip-deep in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> material, but I really want to go hog-wild with Evocations when I get to play in a proper game rather than a playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome at my table, Eric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T04:06:35-08:00","id":388293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388181#post388181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it's because I've spent months hip-deep in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> material, but I really want to go hog-wild with Evocations when I get to play in a proper game rather than a playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, hey! I don't have an rpg.net account so I can't post on the Ask the Devs thread there, but since you might or might not still be reading this thread, d'you think you could ask Holden/John about giving an example of a non-jade artifact weapon? I mean, the ones I can remember being talked about are the volcano sword, the hurricane sword and the poison sword, which are all pretty elemental. How about something orichalcum or starmetal or something? Pretty please with sugar on top?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T04:48:59-08:00","id":388321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388176#post388176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that the other way around, here a quote by John from the Ask the Dev thread:</div> </div> </div> </div>From the same thread: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Solar Charm set does indeed lack any Charm (that I can remember off the top of my head) as singularly jaw-dropping as Volcano Cutter\u2019s final published Evocation, All Creation Turns to Ash[1]. (Yes, we extended the cascade by one more effect.) ACTtA does\u2026 not quite what it says on the tin, but change the name to \u201cHey, Where\u2019d Nighthammer District Go?\u201d and you\u2019re pretty close.<br /> <br /> But if you don\u2019t have fundamental combat skills, you will never, ever, ever manage to actually perform the necessary set-up for that Evocation\u2019s deployment, much less use it without killing yourself and your whole Circle in the process.<br /> <br /> [1] Except maybe Wyld-Shaping Technique. </div> </div> </div> and <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to rock a character with nothing but Evocations is a bit like playing Street Fighter, picking Ryu, and trying to win using no moves other than the dragon punch. Unlessyour opponent forgot to plug his controller in, that is not going to work out for you. </div> </div> </div>That suggests to me that yes, evocations without the required base skills are weaker then the &quot;pure&quot; base skills, but if you mix these base skills with evocation, you come out ahead - So, given an equal level of XP, daiclave evocations alone are weaker (because they can't be used) then melee charms alone, but either of these are weaker than a proper balance between daiclave evocations and melee charms.<br /> <br /> 'Course, &quot;Stronger&quot; in this case also depends on what kind of situation you're in. If you don't want to burn down everything around you, &quot;All Creation Turns to Ash&quot; might not be the effect you want to use. So, &quot;Situational to some degree&quot; is another factor for evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 02-01-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T08:26:25-08:00","id":388463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, &quot;Spend motes and solve plots&quot; Charms are terrible game design. I'm hoping that they stuck to their guns and eliminted as many of those as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider &quot;not being disarmed&quot; on a quite different level than Judge's Ear or TID.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could answer your question with a question: how is a game fun <i>without</i> risk and challenge? You put Artifact dots and Charms into your daiklave? That's fine, but you're taking the risk that it'll get nicked or destroyed. Unless Evocations are stupidly overpowerdly broken, I don't see the risk:reward of them panning out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no commensurate risk with normal Charms or Spells, and your balance point there is what exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if a player takes Tiger Warrior Training, is it then not okay for an adversary to attack their troops? They invested time and a Charm into getting those troops. If they have farmland or trade caravans, can the antagonist not burn or pillage them? Why is it okay to attack one aspect of an enemy's infrastructure, but not another?</div> </div> </div> </div>As was pointed out above, this is a false equivalency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the enemy in question has the time, resources, motivation and temperant to steal the Sword of Omens, why should they not? It's a legit attack vector. Your monster of the week shouldn't be going after the Sword of Omens, but Mum-Ra sure as hell should be...Lion-o without the Sword is much less of a threat than Lion-o with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't believe I said it should never be a plot, just not a recurring plot. Mumm-Ra doing it successfully, once, and still not being able to beat Lion-O is one thing; the Lunatacs doing it every episode is quite another. That quickly devolves into Team Rocket Wants This One Pikachu territory, and it becomes a joke instead of a real plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so do I. I'm just saying I feel that Evocations are comparatively risky investment. I don't know if I would say <i>bad</i> investment just yet. Playing equipment dependent characters in the past has taught me that, if at all possible, you should never have any piece or set of equipment that's so precious as to be irreplacable, because the general chaos of the game <i>will</i> practically ensure you'll be without them at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's a table thing for you then. I've never had that experience; if I ever left gear behind, it was for purposeful reasons of infeasibility, not my ST constantly trying to steal my toys.<br /> <br /> And again it's a pretty fringe case if you invest all normal and Solar XP into Evocations on one weapon. Diversification of your portfolio is the best way to not be denied power applicability in a situation. If all you have is a magic hammer, everything looks like a nail, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:00:09-08:00","id":388482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388321#post388321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That suggests to me that yes, evocations without the required base skills are weaker then the &quot;pure&quot; base skills, but if you mix these base skills with evocation, you come out ahead - So, given an equal level of XP, daiclave evocations alone are weaker (because they can't be used) then melee charms alone, but either of these are weaker than a proper balance between daiclave evocations and melee charms.<br /> <br /> 'Course, &quot;Stronger&quot; in this case also depends on what kind of situation you're in. If you don't want to burn down everything around you, &quot;All Creation Turns to Ash&quot; might not be the effect you want to use. So, &quot;Situational to some degree&quot; is another factor for evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't take it this way at all. I took Holden/John's comments to mean, trying to use just evocations with a daiklave won't work because you need skills in melee to wield the sword. For the &quot;All Creation Turns to Ash&quot; evocation, it may need you to have built up substantial Momentum (can't remember if this is the right name for the power you build up in combat in 3E) before you can use the evocation. If that's the case, having no melee charms will make it difficult to build up enough Momentum to even use ACTtA. Also, if your lacking in a base Melee skill, your not going to even be able to build any momentum and are likely going to get yourself killed.<br /> In essence, if you can't fight well with your weapon, then Evocations are probably not going to be that useful to you. This is how I interpreted what the devs were trying to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:27:33-08:00","id":388495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388131#post388131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That might kind of work for sorcery, but it seems really unfeasable for Evocations. You don't comprehensively master the power of a weapon by being no good at fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This said, the Melee 5, Speciality +3 person with no Melee Charms *is* good, to say the least, at fighting. Whether or not &quot;Awesome like the world's greatest mortal plus high power flashy evocations&quot; is actually a practical way to win fights though.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:36:11-08:00","id":388497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387760#post387760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't pay XP for the tiger warriors (probably, unless your ST makes you pay XP for things you earn through in story actions), you paid XP to gain the ability to make tiger warriors and can continue to train more if some of them get destroyed. A more accurate analogy would be if your ST declared that your opponent had somehow made it so that you are incapable of training new tiger warriors and that charm you spent XP on is useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, second scenario: the Command background. If I take a single dot, do I have five invincible guys following me around? Is every level 1 Manse an impregnable fortress that can't be bombed, sabotaged or captured? Allies can never be capture, Mentors can never be killed?<br /> <br /> I'm being a bit hyperbolic here, but I'm really trying to understand this argument that you can't fuck with something just because a player paid Background dots/Merit shekels/whatever for it. If that's the case, it's so unbelievably broken a concept I'm surprised that the game doesn't implode under the sheer absurdity of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387791#post387791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the power to incinerate cities might be worth the risks, that the indestructibility of Artifacts makes the risk of the thing being broken in about the same area as the risk of one's character dying, if not even harder, and that having the Artifact stolen can be a suitable plot development for efforts to get it back, so long as the ST is not frustrating and arbitrary about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'll depend on how Evocations end up looking. I think your &quot;average&quot; daiklave isn't going to near as crazy as Volcano Cutter.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm not advocating that the Dawn's magic pokey stick gets stolen every adventure. But it is a point of vulnerability...your killstick gets taken away, you're at a severe disadvantage. I dunno. Maybe I'm too used to playing games like Shadowrun, where if you're a street sammie it's pretty much a given that your ware will get turned off at some point, so you better have a back up plan. The idea that Ares would play nice and not try that would get you laughed off of Shadowland.<br /> <br /> (As an incidental note, I'm playing a hacker in a Spycraft game at the moment, which is an absolutely terrible system but whatevs, and I have a main computer, a backup, and a back up to the back up because I feel it'd be intensely stupid if the terrorist organization we're running down <i>didn't</i> try to neutralize me at some point. And I also have burly companions in case they try to just shoot me in the face or something.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388463#post388463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no commensurate risk with normal Charms or Spells, and your balance point there is what exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does there need to be a balance point?<br /> <br /> I mean, it's the exact same situation for NPCs. If the PCs manage to swipe Excaliber or destroy Mjolnir, than their wielders are in just as much trouble as a PC who invests heavily in a weapon and loses it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe that's a table thing for you then. I've never had that experience; if I ever left gear behind, it was for purposeful reasons of infeasibility, not my ST constantly trying to steal my toys. </div> </div> </div>My table thing is that the PCs don't get special treatment because they're PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T10:24:46-08:00","id":388597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388293#post388293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, hey! I don't have an rpg.net account so I can't post on the Ask the Devs thread there, but since you might or might not still be reading this thread, d'you think you could ask Holden/John about giving an example of a non-jade artifact weapon? I mean, the ones I can remember being talked about are the volcano sword, the hurricane sword and the poison sword, which are all pretty elemental. How about something orichalcum or starmetal or something? Pretty please with sugar on top?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stormcaller, the daiklave that summons a mounting tempest every second it is drawn, is actually orichalcum.<br /> <br /> Black Wind, which Holden mentioned in the rpg thread, is a soulsteel skycutter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T10:39:01-08:00","id":388605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388133#post388133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless something has changed, we totally know that. When they gave us an artifacts evocation tree a sizeable chunk of it was locked behind a solar charm (call the blade) as a prerequisite to learning them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/804449\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...n/posts/804449</a><br /> <br /> I count 7 evocations in the cascade that starts with call the blade. So even assuming that, hypothetically speaking, another type of exalt could learn 3rd tier evocations they still won't be as good with it as a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't deny this is a plausible way for things to turn out. But scroll up a bit from that graphic: what's shown is just an example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 Kickstarter Update</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike the &quot;set&quot; progression of martial arts trees or the unchanging nature of spells, Evocation arrays are flexible, born of a synthesis of the construction and history of a daiklave, and the expertise and spirit of the one who wields it. ... As such, <b>all published Evocation arrays are intended to act as base-line suggestions</b> which players should feel free to add to, elaborate on, or customize as their game progresses and they become a part of their weapon's storied history, and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that they've said two Solars can't necessarily pull out the same Evocations. Given Solars will be the only ones yet published, it makes sense to give example arrays that will be useful to them -- including an example where a Charm serves as a prerequisite. It wouldn't strain my belief at all for a member of another splat to use one of their own Charms to qualify for later Evocations, and it's plausible such examples might appear in their books. Their players may have to do more tweaking or homebrewing of effects for earlier ones, especially if the splat lacks a Charm that would analogue well for what's written, but that's a different story. We just don't yet know what the limitations are for each splat.<br /> <br /> To be clear, my argument isn't &quot;some non-Solars will very definitely get Adamant Evocations,&quot; just that &quot;it's not a certainty at this point Solars alone will get Adamant Evocations.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'll depend on how Evocations end up looking. I think your &quot;average&quot; daiklave isn't going to near as crazy as Volcano Cutter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as there can be said to be a norm, Volcano Cutter seems to be it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Volcano Cutter is intended to be an example of &quot;your average, bog-standard daiklave.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T11:13:52-08:00","id":388642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388597#post388597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stormcaller, the daiklave that summons a mounting tempest every second it is drawn, is actually orichalcum.<br /> <br /> Black Wind, which Holden mentioned in the rpg thread, is a soulsteel skycutter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Why not Blue Jade for Stormcaller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T11:37:21-08:00","id":388665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388605#post388605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, my argument isn't &quot;some non-Solars will very definitely get Adamant Evocations,&quot; just that &quot;it's not a certainty at this point Solars alone will get Adamant Evocations.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that seems apparent to me. I can't remember which post it was, but it was heavily implied that Dragonbloods could access Adamant Evocations with their flavored Jade artifacts (ie Red Jade for Fire Aspects, Black Jade for Water Aspects, etc). I would also &quot;guess&quot; that Lunars and Sidereals can access Adamant Evocations from their favored material artifacts as well. The &quot;Solars are undisputed at evocations&quot; I believe stems solely from the fact that they can access those Adamant Evocations regardless of what the material the artifact is made of. That's just the feeling I'm getting from the Devs at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388605#post388605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Why not Blue Jade for Stormcaller?</div> </div> </div> </div>We could make a guess, but that's all it would be at this point. My guess, most Jade weapons are made by Dragonbloods. They aren't nearly as skilled of craftsman as the Solars are, and a weapon like Stormcaller seems almost like a strategic weapon (aka beyond a Dragonbloods ability to craft). This is just a guess though, and is about as valid as &quot;it's made of orichalcum and not blue/black jade because... it just is!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T11:41:43-08:00","id":388668,"title":"","content":"Orichalcum is &quot;full of sorcerous power&quot;, so I'd guess something about how Stormcaller works has the flavour of sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:01:55-08:00","id":388683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well that seems apparent to me. I can't remember which post it was, but it was heavily implied that Dragonbloods could access Adamant Evocations with their flavored Jade artifacts (ie Red Jade for Fire Aspects, Black Jade for Water Aspects, etc). I would also &quot;guess&quot; that Lunars and Sidereals can access Adamant Evocations from their favored material artifacts as well. The &quot;Solars are undisputed at evocations&quot; I believe stems solely from the fact that they can access those Adamant Evocations regardless of what the material the artifact is made of. That's just the feeling I'm getting from the Devs at the moment. </div> </div> </div>Again, assuming nothing has changed, it was once stated that Sidereal exalted are going to be the worst at using evocations out of all the classic exalted. I'm guessing that they will be limited to emerald tier evocations on everything but their own magical material but will will be able to access sapphire evocations on Starmetal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:01:58-08:00","id":388684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388642#post388642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Why not Blue Jade for Stormcaller?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it will be self-evident once you've read the descriptions of the magical materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:12:15-08:00","id":388714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=387756#post387756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so do I. I'm just saying I feel that Evocations are comparatively risky investment. I don't know if I would say <i>bad</i> investment just yet. Playing equipment dependent characters in the past has taught me that, if at all possible, you should never have any piece or set of equipment that's so precious as to be irreplacable, because the general chaos of the game <i>will</i> practically ensure you'll be without them at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and the more you pump into that signature weapon, the more you stand to lose if it's taken from you.<br /> <br /> Though I'm not sure it's more risky than other common choices players make like creating a social character with only the basic combat charms, or pouring time/energy into crafts, developing an organization or kingdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:16:33-08:00","id":388715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388120#post388120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Martial arts are more interesting to me on other splats then they are on solars for some reason, possibly because there are more splats that can access SMA then their are that can access top tier evocations and top tier sorcery (from what we know only solars get top tier evocations and if it follows 2E then the only other exalt type with access to 3rd circle sorcery will be infernals).</div> </div> </div> </div>Um okay. Though I find the ideas about splats that can access SMA odd since we really do not know yet. I am going to wait and see and stick to my enthusiasm for kung fu in a kung fu world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:48:17-08:00","id":388768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388715#post388715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um okay. Though I find the ideas about splats that can access SMA odd since we really do not know yet. I am going to wait and see and stick to my enthusiasm for kung fu in a kung fu world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for the sake of providing a list...<br /> <br /> Sidereals can create and teach SMA (goes without saying), Solars can learn SMA from a sifu (same as last edition), and it's been mentioned that Getimians can also learn SMA. It's unclear where the latter falls on the &quot;can create them,&quot; and &quot;need to learn from a sifu&quot; continuum. Or whether they fall outside it.<br /> <br /> At last word, the rest of the classic splats cannot (so Lunars, Dragonblooded, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and probably Infernals). It's unclear if there are any other New Challengers Approaching who are capable of it. There is presumably nothing barring particular Exigents from it, should it suit their particular themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals and Solars can learn SMA. None of the other classic splats. SMA is going to be the Sidereal's highest expression of the martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:48:29-08:00","id":388769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388668#post388668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum is &quot;full of sorcerous power&quot;, so I'd guess something about how Stormcaller works has the flavour of sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be this as well, blue jade lets you shoot lightning, orichalcum lets you call forth a tempest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:51:29-08:00","id":388773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, second scenario: the Command background. If I take a single dot, do I have five invincible guys following me around? Is every level 1 Manse an impregnable fortress that can't be bombed, sabotaged or captured? Allies can never be capture, Mentors can never be killed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not what is being said. It's the notion that, if one of these things happens to you, you're not just out the experience point investment forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being a bit hyperbolic here,</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for admitting that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I'm really trying to understand this argument that you can't fuck with something just because a player paid Background dots/Merit shekels/whatever for it. If that's the case, it's so unbelievably broken a concept I'm surprised that the game doesn't implode under the sheer absurdity of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that you can't fuck with it, it's that (1) it looks punitive if you constantly do this, no matter how much sense it would make, especially if some characters have no places like this that are open for easy targeting; (2) if someone pays 10 XP for something cool and that cool thing is removed, you just say &quot;welp, bad investment, suck it up?&quot; I'm not in favor of that, especially if that investment can never be recouped, it creates bad feelings. Especially if, as I already said, some people invest in stuff that is easier to strip from them, versus the barehanded sorcerer not really caring about gear or friends as much as the sword-wielding warrior who leads a tribe of berserkers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'll depend on how Evocations end up looking. I think your &quot;average&quot; daiklave isn't going to near as crazy as Volcano Cutter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Volcano Cutter was noted as being an example of an &quot;average&quot; daiklave, actually...as much as there is such a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, I'm not advocating that the Dawn's magic pokey stick gets stolen every adventure. But it is a point of vulnerability...your killstick gets taken away, you're at a severe disadvantage. I dunno. Maybe I'm too used to playing games like Shadowrun, where if you're a street sammie it's pretty much a given that your ware will get turned off at some point, so you better have a back up plan. The idea that Ares would play nice and not try that would get you laughed off of Shadowland.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, but there's also quite a difference in tone and genre between the games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does there need to be a balance point?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Evocations are per se worse just because you can have the item stolen without any meta-recompense, then they're a much worse potential investment by comparison, because knowledge of Charms, Spells and MA techniques can't be stolen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388497#post388497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My table thing is that the PCs don't get special treatment because they're PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this is only weird because PCs are clearly special. They experience a rate of power growth and status that requires suspension of disbelief or it's simply not credible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-01-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:56:57-08:00","id":388779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At last word, the rest of the classic splats cannot (so Lunars, Dragonblooded, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and probably Infernals). It's unclear if there are any other New Challengers Approaching who are capable of it. There is presumably nothing barring particular Exigents from it, should it suit their particular themes. </div> </div> </div>It has been said that Getimian exalts will be able to learn SMA (and that Rakan Thulio thinks they are better at it then Sidereals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:17:58-08:00","id":388800,"title":"","content":"I feel as though &quot;investment&quot; is a really weird way to look on purchases with XP. I also think that such things are going to be necessarily secured by the same kind of social contract that says you can sleep in a bed that wasn't made from grenades; I mean, I think XP refunds are as likely to stop an ST from being a dick as being able to return to life stopped Christ from getting his head pounded in in that one Robot Chicken sketch. And if it wasn't arbitrary, and was fitting to the story, well... an XP refund feels as though it kind of takes the teeth out of it, doesn't it? Like having a love interest die off and then having an immediate replacement jump out of the bushes. I think differentiating things according to how vulnerable they are makes about as much sense as making Sail cheaper than Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:46:45-08:00","id":388843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388769#post388769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess would be this as well, blue jade lets you shoot lightning, orichalcum lets you call forth a tempest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well described, with the distinction being more about tone and feel of the mechanics than scale (because Orichalcum vs Jade weapons are independent of artefact and evocation level).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:54:39-08:00","id":388850,"title":"","content":"I'll note that the Orichalcum Caste is pretty associated with lightning as far as Alchemicals go, so perhaps that has something to do with it. /may be wildly off the mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:08:16-08:00","id":388906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388597#post388597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stormcaller, the daiklave that summons a mounting tempest every second it is drawn, is actually orichalcum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Hm. I guess it can work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388597#post388597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Wind, which Holden mentioned in the rpg thread, is a soulsteel skycutter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but we don't know what it does, only the name! Or did someone mention something about Black Wind's evocations and I just don't remember?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:15:56-08:00","id":388910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388906#post388906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah, but we don't know what it does, only the name! Or did someone mention something about Black Wind's evocations and I just don't remember?</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:21:44-08:00","id":388919,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a weapon based around calling up an actual volcano to erupt might feel distinct from Volcano Cutter and also be orichalcum...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:24:39-08:00","id":388920,"title":"","content":"Is everyone just ignoring the part where the devs said that, <i>worst</i> case scenario, you'd simply get your XP back if you completely lost access to your artefact and its evocations? <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/763\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the Nishkriya link.</a>.<br /> <br /> This obviously means &quot;messing with them&quot; is expected by the devs. Next on my list is...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388482#post388482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't take it this way at all. I took Holden/John's comments to mean, trying to use just evocations with a daiklave won't work because you need skills in melee to wield the sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually pretty much what I meant. &quot;Weaker&quot; must not always mean &quot;less effect when used&quot;, it can also mean &quot;less likely to be possible to use&quot; if you get a bit creative with interpretations. In any case, to be able to use a daiclave's evocation to full effect, you'll have to have good melee skills already, or the evocations are wasted on you. Hence, &quot;Just evocations&quot; is weak, but &quot;Balance between Evocations and Charms&quot; is stronger than charms alone. <br /> <br /> Which together leads me to... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388463#post388463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no commensurate risk with normal Charms or Spells, and your balance point there is what exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as I understand it, Evocations (+ the required attributes and charms to back them up) are more effective, XP-wise, than only investing in charms and attributes - you get more power per XP, with the price that it's power that can be taken from you, if only temporarily. (But only temporarily, because, as pointed out, <i>permanently</i> using access to your evocations would mean you get your XP back. And &quot;Re-building a destroyed daiclave&quot; is also explicitly pointed out as possible.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:28:50-08:00","id":388924,"title":"","content":"Another thing on the evocation front, they aren't just going to be on weapons. They can also be on artifacts that are much harder to steal, like your armor. Also, some weapons are pretty damn hard to steal anyway, like a smash fist or god-kicking boots","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:35:03-08:00","id":388930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388800#post388800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though &quot;investment&quot; is a really weird way to look on purchases with XP. I also think that such things are going to be necessarily secured by the same kind of social contract that says you can sleep in a bed that wasn't made from grenades; I mean, I think XP refunds are as likely to stop an ST from being a dick as being able to return to life stopped Christ from getting his head pounded in in that one Robot Chicken sketch. And if it wasn't arbitrary, and was fitting to the story, well... an XP refund feels as though it kind of takes the teeth out of it, doesn't it? Like having a love interest die off and then having an immediate replacement jump out of the bushes. I think differentiating things according to how vulnerable they are makes about as much sense as making Sail cheaper than Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what your saying about taking the &quot;teeth outta the game&quot;. However, we're not talking about a loss of say 10-20 XP here. Someone heavily invested in Evocations for their weapon could be 100+ XP deep. Now IF I were to take away his weapon in game as part of a plot... I would then be completed justified by informing his fellow Circle sorcerer and martial artist that crazy spirits visited them in their dreams one night. When they woke up they have lost 100+ XP worth of MA training and spells! Balance can be a bitch, but I'm not going to completely screw over one of my PCs without spreading the &quot;fun&quot;. Any GM/ST that does that isn't worth a shit in any game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:41:47-08:00","id":388935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388919#post388919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a weapon based around calling up an actual volcano to erupt might feel distinct from Volcano Cutter and also be orichalcum...</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Stormcaller orichalcum, and it conjures an actual hurricane? Same principle really, though that begs the question why Volcano Cutter isn't red jade (or is it? I forget).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:45:57-08:00","id":388940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388924#post388924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing on the evocation front, they aren't just going to be on weapons. They can also be on artifacts that are much harder to steal, like your armor. Also, some weapons are pretty damn hard to steal anyway, like a smash fist or god-kicking boots</div> </div> </div> </div>Some examples of Armor Evocations would be awesome to have. Weapons get all of the love and it just isn't fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:49:26-08:00","id":388966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388935#post388935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Stormcaller orichalcum, and it conjures an actual hurricane? Same principle really, though that begs the question why Volcano Cutter isn't red jade (or is it? I forget).</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the kickstarter preview Volcano Cutter is 'primarily' red jade but doesn't mention what else is in it.<br /> <br /> Edit: No wait, yes it does. The other part is white jade, which makes sense (earth+fire=lava)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><b