lost the weapon because he was an idiot? Or what if an Abyssal cut off his sword arm? Or what if someone simply killed him?<br /> <br /> How would you balance that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T01:24:57-08:00","id":389538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388935#post388935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Stormcaller orichalcum, and it conjures an actual hurricane? Same principle really</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not it is the same principle is what I was asking, as trying to develop a basis for what might be distinct between a sorcerous effect and an elemental one.<br /> <br /> It certainly gives me a sense of orichalcum as the most suitable material to use for demonic weapons, at least.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:10:27-08:00","id":389805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389536#post389536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if he lost the weapon because he was an idiot? Or what if an Abyssal cut off his sword arm? Or what if someone simply killed him?<br /> <br /> How would you balance that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did specifically say &quot;take away his weapon as part of a <b>plot</b>&quot;. Losing your weapon because your an idiot is not a plot device. Nor is having an Abyssal cut your arm off (though losing an arm doesn't preclude you from using your off-hand to retrieve your weapon). As for dead, come on Jutlander, now you're just being silly.<br /> <br /> I will point out that 2E specifically mentioned that if a single PC in a group dies, you can award a commensurate amount of XP to them for character creation to maintain overall balance and &quot;fun&quot; within the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:16:51-08:00","id":389807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389538#post389538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whether or not it is the same principle is what I was asking, as trying to develop a basis for what might be distinct between a sorcerous effect and an elemental one.<br /> <br /> It certainly gives me a sense of orichalcum as the most suitable material to use for demonic weapons, at least.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the material most associated with the Unconquered Sun being the &quot;demonic material of choice&quot;. Not to say that it couldn't, just that it's almost certainly not the most suitable. I would imagine Brass and/or Malfean Iron are the likely demon associated materials. Just going out on a limb here, but it would definitely make more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:34:12-08:00","id":389832,"title":"","content":"For those of you who are super excited about martial arts, but not so much evocations: imagine your favorite martial art. Like say, a style that uses a spear and shield.<br /> <br /> Now imagine mastering that style with an artifact spear or shield that has evocations to go with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:46:29-08:00","id":389839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389832#post389832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of you who are super excited about martial arts, but not so much evocations: imagine your favorite martial art. Like say, a style that uses a spear and shield.<br /> <br /> Now imagine mastering that style with an artifact spear or shield that has evocations to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>John, you tease!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">I'truth, I'm actually already very excited about Evocations, so the post is less to my benefit than it might be to others, but it's still left me rather excited.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:55:10-08:00","id":389844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389839#post389839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John, you tease!</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly what alucard said.. man that's made me start thinking XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:10:06-08:00","id":389856,"title":"","content":"I wonder why everyone is treating the evocations vs charms as an either/or thing. You can't even spend half your experience on Solar charms, so you're either buffing evocations, MA, sorcery or attributes anyways. Use all your regular xp on Solar charms, but as a meleeist the choice isn't between more Solar charms or evocations, it's between evocations and attribute dots!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:17:30-08:00","id":389863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389856#post389856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why everyone is treating the evocations vs charms as an either/or thing. You can't even spend half your experience on Solar charms, so you're either buffing evocations, MA, sorcery or attributes anyways. Use all your regular xp on Solar charms, but as a meleeist the choice isn't between more Solar charms or evocations, it's between evocations and attribute dots!</div> </div> </div> </div>ill be honest thought of using charms and evocations, using something like iron raptor tech and the volcano cutter, to cause mini volcanos at range seems plausible....my brain blanked using evocations with martial arts though XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:00:35-08:00","id":389918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389807#post389807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the material most associated with the Unconquered Sun being the &quot;demonic material of choice&quot;. Not to say that it couldn't, just that it's almost certainly not the most suitable. I would imagine Brass and/or Malfean Iron are the likely demon associated materials. Just going out on a limb here, but it would definitely make more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do brass and Malfean Iron count as Magical Materials?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:46:25-08:00","id":389954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389856#post389856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why everyone is treating the evocations vs charms as an either/or thing. You can't even spend half your experience on Solar charms, so you're either buffing evocations, MA, sorcery or attributes anyways. Use all your regular xp on Solar charms, but as a meleeist the choice isn't between more Solar charms or evocations, it's between evocations and attribute dots!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of on topic, with Solar XP, I can see where that would work for combat focused characters, it does seem odd for social focused characters who concept does not include sorcery or combat, since evocations and MA look like combat abilities, so they either have great dots or have sorcery or get evocations. Of course a lot of social only characters will be Eclipses, so they've got one more avenue there. Or maybe this isn't an issue because of how Solar XP works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:58:33-08:00","id":389985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389918#post389918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do brass and Malfean Iron count as Magical Materials?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 3E... I have no idea. In 2E several Infernal artifacts were made out of them, though I'm not sure if that means they were classified as magical materials (don't have my books in front of me to check). It's more that demons seem to have a preference of working with brass and malfean iron. While Orichalcum, the material associated closely with UCS created with the power of the Sun and gold, tends to have strong &quot;bane to creatures of darkness&quot; themes. Creatures of darkness include all demons, the dead/undead, and fey. Once again I'm not saying no Orichalcum artifacts will have some demon themes. Just that it's probably far and away the preferred material for demon themes.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I could very well be completely wrong for 3E. Though it would require a rewrite to Orichalcum as a whole to make it the preferred material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T10:05:49-08:00","id":389998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389832#post389832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of you who are super excited about martial arts, but not so much evocations: imagine your favorite martial art. Like say, a style that uses a spear and shield.<br /> <br /> Now imagine mastering that style with an artifact spear or shield that has evocations to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is an awesome depiction! I'm also a little confused. I thought 3E intended to move away from the &quot;every weapon style needs it's own martial art&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T12:20:09-08:00","id":390198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389954#post389954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of on topic, with Solar XP, I can see where that would work for combat focused characters, it does seem odd for social focused characters who concept does not include sorcery or combat, since evocations and MA look like combat abilities, so they either have great dots or have sorcery or get evocations. Of course a lot of social only characters will be Eclipses, so they've got one more avenue there. Or maybe this isn't an issue because of how Solar XP works?</div> </div> </div> </div>There will always be non-combat evocations, I guess? Or if you are really dead set on your character not branching out and learning any of those things you could just not spend the solar XP once you have finished using it to max out your social attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:47:27-08:00","id":390305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389832#post389832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of you who are super excited about martial arts, but not so much evocations: imagine your favorite martial art. Like say, a style that uses a spear and shield.<br /> <br /> Now imagine mastering that style with an artifact spear or shield that has evocations to go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Evocations is that I'm not sure what all I can do with them*.<br /> <br /> I've seen elemental-ish powers suggested as well as references to video games I haven't played (Kingdom Hearts and Final Fantasy.) Because we've had two editions worth of martial arts and sorcery, it's easier for me to imagine dozens of different and unique things my PC could do with access to them.<br /> <br /> If my PC does favors the spear and secures herself an artifact one, what sort of powers might it have?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389998#post389998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While that is an awesome depiction! I'm also a little confused. I thought 3E intended to move away from the &quot;every weapon style needs it's own martial art&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned that specific combination up-thread. I don't think that's confirmation of a martial art specifically for spear and shield.<br /> <br /> *Which may be my fault, I haven't kept up-to-date with all the information out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:53:02-08:00","id":390312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the material most associated with the Unconquered Sun being the &quot;demonic material of choice&quot;. Not to say that it couldn't, just that it's almost certainly not the most suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Associated with the Unconquered Sun? Maybe not. Associated with sorcery? Fits more than anything else. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine Brass and/or Malfean Iron are the likely demon associated materials.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd have them as well! Same as how whatever Prince Diamond's daiklave does requires Chiaruscuro glass. Still wouldn't have a daiklave made entirely of glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:02:57-08:00","id":390319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390305#post390305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about Evocations is that I'm not sure what all I can do with them*.<br /> <br /> I've seen elemental-ish powers suggested as well as references to video games I haven't played (Kingdom Hearts and Final Fantasy.) Because we've had two editions worth of martial arts and sorcery, it's easier for me to imagine dozens of different and unique things my PC could do with access to them.<br /> <br /> If my PC does favors the spear and secures herself an artifact one, what sort of powers might it have?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mentioned that specific combination up-thread. I don't think that's confirmation of a martial art specifically for spear and shield.<br /> <br /> *Which may be my fault, I haven't kept up-to-date with all the information out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they have mentioned a spear that has an evocation which allows you to fly. And someone asked about making a mirror which did things like create illusions and such and they said that was totally something you could do with evocations. They also said a sword having an evocation which allowed you to remotely control it as if you had telekinesis could be a thing you do.<br /> <br /> edit: Oh, and someone asked about making an artifact version of an unorthodox weapon like a piece of cookware and it was mentioned that, by default, such a thing would probably have evocations related to cooking food.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, basically you can do pretty much anything with evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-02-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:09:34-08:00","id":390440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389954#post389954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of on topic, with Solar XP, I can see where that would work for combat focused characters, it does seem odd for social focused characters who concept does not include sorcery or combat, since evocations and MA look like combat abilities, so they either have great dots or have sorcery or get evocations. Of course a lot of social only characters will be Eclipses, so they've got one more avenue there. Or maybe this isn't an issue because of how Solar XP works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, but I somewhat rarely see absolutely 100% pure social or mental characters anyway. The ones who do are probably going to just have crazy attributes or maybe there's something else to spend that xp on. On the other hand usually I see characters who go like, 90% into social or medicine or something, but still pick up a few fighting charms just because Creation is a place where kung-fu happens rather frequently and it's fun to participate in cool ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:38:25-08:00","id":390513,"title":"","content":"Yo dawg, I heard you like sorcery so I enchanted your quill to automatically correct your misspellings and hire actors for you, so you can spell while you spell and cast while you cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:39:15-08:00","id":390514,"title":"","content":"I think there was a reference to a dire lance that did something invoking the image of a giant acupuncture needle...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T16:11:42-08:00","id":390556,"title":"","content":"True enough - there's some of that &quot;kung fu&quot; world aspect where being pushed towards some combat could be desirable and there's non-combat evocations (at least some of them). It seems like it might change the balance of characters who people are playing a bit though? Presumably the playtests haven't been inundated with people frowning that the system feels like it is giving them incentives towards characters who weaken their concept, so presumably it all tends to work out OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:11:26-08:00","id":390648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390312#post390312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Associated with the Unconquered Sun? Maybe not. Associated with sorcery? Fits more than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the magical material orichalcum is not associated with the Unconquered Sun? The same orichalcum that requires the sun's power specifically to make, which is used in nearly every &quot;Bane to Creatures of Darkness&quot; artifact, in which UCS is clothed at least partially in molten orichalcum, and in which it was said that UCS's blood is molten orichalcum.... is NOT associated with the Unconquered Sun! If orichalcum has received a substantial rewrite, then that's fine. However, until we see such a rewrite you're going to have a hard time... no an impossible time convincing me it's the preferred material for demon themes. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:18:09-08:00","id":390677,"title":"","content":"Considering Volfer's sword was 'twisted' into being a demonic thing, it seems unlikely that baseline orichalcum is the material of demon stuff. If it was then being bathed in the angry death cursed blood of a demon wouldn't have really done anything to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T20:59:05-08:00","id":390972,"title":"","content":"I really hope that there is some kind of Synergy between all three of the exotic magics, and not just Martial Arts and Evocations. I'd love to Heaven Thunder Hammer a guy in to a group of his cronies, and then immediately follow it up with a Death of Obsidian Butterflies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:23:37-08:00","id":390985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390972#post390972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope that there is some kind of Synergy between all three of the exotic magics, and not just Martial Arts and Evocations. I'd love to Heaven Thunder Hammer a guy in to a group of his cronies, and then immediately follow it up with a Death of Obsidian Butterflies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, Heaven Thunder Hammer <i>was</i> in Solar Hero Style, wasn't it? Meaning it'd now be in Solar Brawl, and thus technically not a Martial Art.<br /> *attempts to shield himself with his own pedantry*<br /> <br /> But yeah, I feel there'd be some natural synergy in places. Wood Dragon's Claw plus Invulnerable Skin of Bronze plus Brawl or a barehanded Martial Art sounds like a pretty dangerous combo. I get the sense that it'd just depend on the particular Evocations, Spells, and Martial Arts. Like, let's say Volcano Cutter has a few Evocations that are easier to use or more potent if there's a pre-existing source of lava or magma, and can intensify any that is. It's a little flavorful bonus, but not super amazing on its own, and tricky to exploit. Unless you know how to summon a Magma Kraken. Then it's just all kinds of ridiculous.<br /> <br /> And of course different &quot;styles&quot; of Sorcery have access to different options for gathering motes. Necromancy sounds like it'd really lend itself to options that draw on blood and souls. And wouldn't ya know it, John's made mention that Soulsteel Evocations &quot;[reap] blood and souls!&quot; Potentially, that could be like a match made in the Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:25:32-08:00","id":390991,"title":"","content":"Magma Kraken fist would be amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T23:38:17-08:00","id":391102,"title":"","content":"Considering how Martial Arts are seen as a path to enlightenment in most kung fu stories, I would be shocked if there wasn't a Sorcerous Initiation that somehow key off of punching a dude with your enlightened fist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T00:59:05-08:00","id":391135,"title":"","content":"Not just for Solars, but I'm most stoked about Evocations. Lately I've been thinking of weird artifacts and what sort of evocations they might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T01:21:59-08:00","id":391145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390648#post390648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the magical material orichalcum is not associated with the Unconquered Sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>...No. Such associations might be irrelevant to what I'm talking about, though.<br /> <br /> Tell me, what do you think is the big association with the Unconquered Sun evident in a daiklave that summons hurricanes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">no an impossible time convincing me it's the preferred material for demon themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery is the preferred thing for non-Infernal Exalted controlling demonic powers, whether they be actual demons or things like Total Annihilation.<br /> <br /> Orichalcum on its own probably won't do it. Orichalcum alloyed with Malfean brass, or forged in some captured fire of Ligier, or quenched in vitriol, or beaten with a hammer made from one of the stolen bones of Florivet, or worked in the Forge of Night...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T07:56:33-08:00","id":391437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390648#post390648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the magical material orichalcum is not associated with the Unconquered Sun? The same orichalcum that requires the sun's power specifically to make, which is used in nearly every &quot;Bane to Creatures of Darkness&quot; artifact, in which UCS is clothed at least partially in molten orichalcum, and in which it was said that UCS's blood is molten orichalcum.... is NOT associated with the Unconquered Sun! If orichalcum has received a substantial rewrite, then that's fine. However, until we see such a rewrite you're going to have a hard time... no an impossible time convincing me it's the preferred material for demon themes.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It probably worked like a charm for Theion artifacts though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:35:19-08:00","id":391459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=390648#post390648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the magical material orichalcum is not associated with the Unconquered Sun? The same orichalcum that requires the sun's power specifically to make, which is used in nearly every &quot;Bane to Creatures of Darkness&quot; artifact, in which UCS is clothed at least partially in molten orichalcum, and in which it was said that UCS's blood is molten orichalcum.... is NOT associated with the Unconquered Sun! If orichalcum has received a substantial rewrite, then that's fine. However, until we see such a rewrite you're going to have a hard time... no an impossible time convincing me it's the preferred material for demon themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's assume that, while other materials can be used in Artifacts, each one requires at least a little of at least one of the Five Magical Materials we know.<br /> <br /> Soulsteel is about the reaping of blood and souls. No relationship with demons.<br /> Jade is about the Five Elements. No relationship with demons.<br /> Starmetal is about inevitability and Fate shenanigans, or something? No apparent relationship with demons.<br /> Moonsilver is about adaptability and other Lunar themes, I'm guessing? No apparent relationship with demons.<br /> Orichalcum is about being infused with sorcerous power. It's by far the most &quot;blank slate&quot; concept of the materials, rather like the Solars themselves, and sorcery does have a conceptual relationship with demons. Now, I don't know how the system works yet, but to me, for flavor, I wouldn't make a pure orichalcum weapon and try to evoke demonic themes with it. Corruption with demonic blood is one possibility, as we know, but if I was deliberately setting out to make a weapon like that, I'd involve iron and brass. We might learn of more interesting options in the core book, or possibly in <i>Arms of the Chosen.</i><br /> <br /> As for my answer to the question... oh, wow. For a character I want to play, Evocations, maybe? My table will probably favor Sorcery, and how that's going to work has been the subject of a lot of discussion around here, and I'll admit that I'm pretty excited. Of the three choices, Martial Arts will probably see the least use at my table, but I'm sure it won't be neglected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:39:45-08:00","id":391464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391145#post391145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...No. Such associations might be irrelevant to what I'm talking about, though.<br /> <br /> Tell me, what do you think is the big association with the Unconquered Sun evident in a daiklave that summons hurricanes?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think orichalcum is logically associated with the Unconquered Sun (in the way that moonsilver is associated with Luna) without every orichalcum Artifact being based around sunlight powers. UCS's themes are excellence, perfection, and frankly, domination (even if it's not tyrannical suzerainty, it's still suzerainty); it makes sense that orichalcum would be the MM built around &quot;dominating&quot; natural effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:41:04-08:00","id":391467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391102#post391102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how Martial Arts are seen as a path to enlightenment in most kung fu stories, I would be shocked if there wasn't a Sorcerous Initiation that somehow key off of punching a dude with your enlightened fist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like initiations will be more than just single one-and-done Charms, probably a short tree with various upgrades. (Or maybe a very large tree, I don't know). It should be straightforward enough for a skilled homebrewer to make an initiation tree and a martial arts style that synergize with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:54:33-08:00","id":391477,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that somebody had already posted up this quote in this thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magical material is the determining factor in the style of Evocations. Red jade will engender a lot of fire magic, while starmetal gives you god magic. Orichalcum is full of sorcerous power, while soulsteel reaps blood and souls. And so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am posting it here because some replies seem to be coming from a place that was unaware of it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, rereading the idea for how Stormcaller works, I wonder if &quot;sorcerous power&quot; might also entail Evocations that require on a need for certain conditions to build up in a manner akin to shaping actions for spells. Evocations in general (or at least Volcano Cutter) do seem to rely on a measure of preamble, from what they've been saying, but perhaps there would be a distinction between them.<br /> <br /> Still, if it's more about being like sorcery shaping than being like spells, it might be that things with an Infernal aspect would be more spread around. I mean, following my prior assumption, it wasn't that you'd get nothing for using Hellish magic to make a weapon from moonsilver or whatever, just less of an image of directly using the demonic magic and more the weapon doing what moonsilver does with a certain organic edge; not just being protean, but shaping itself into a big venomous maw or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:09:22-08:00","id":391491,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Isator Levi;n391477I am posting it here because some replies seem to be coming from a place that was unaware of it.[/QUOTE]<br /> Ah, I had forgotten that, thanks. I just think it'd be a shame of the MM didn't have their divine associations anymore - that would be really strange. But it also fits in a different box from Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:48:05-08:00","id":391624,"title":"","content":"I don't think Magical Materials lack associations with the Incarnae, but that such associations aren't necessarily helpful in describing what they can be used to build.<br /> <br /> Especially if they lead to ideas like &quot;you can't use orichalcum to make something against the Unconquered Sun&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:15:03-08:00","id":391654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=388773#post388773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for admitting that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the examples I give like that are hyperbole. It's occasionally helpful to call attention to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not so much that you can't fuck with it, it's that (1) it looks punitive if you constantly do this, no matter how much sense it would make, especially if some characters have no places like this that are open for easy targeting; (2) if someone pays 10 XP for something cool and that cool thing is removed, you just say &quot;welp, bad investment, suck it up?&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think you may think that I'm advocating Thievy McNightcaste rolling Joe Dawn for his daiklaive straight out of character gen and at the beginning of every adventure, which I'm not. But yeah, if you want to invest in a killstick, that's a risk that's there. Creation is a place where very few people have much incentive to give their opponent a fair fight, particularly if they're going up against a group of Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not in favor of that, especially if that investment can never be recouped, it creates bad feelings. </div> </div> </div>I'm very much of the mind that, if Thievy McNightcaste nicks your killstick, the only time it becomes impossible to get it back is if you die or give up. The former is just how the dice roll sometimes, the latter is your own fault. Thievy ran off? You can chase him. Thievy tossed your killstick into the Crack of Doom? Gird up some Resistance Charms and start dreddging the lava for the bits, then reforge it.<br /> <br /> You're fucking Exalted. Act like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Volcano Cutter was noted as being an example of an &quot;average&quot; daiklave, actually...as much as there is such a thing. </div> </div> </div>Urrghh. Well, depending on implementation, I may just ditch Evocations entirely. I have enough to do running the entire damn world, I don't want to get bogged down having to write up 30 Charms for every jade nail file in Creation.<br /> <br /> (See, that was hyperbole again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Evocations are per se worse just because you can have the item stolen without any meta-recompense... </div> </div> </div>Like I said before, my games (and every game I've played in) at least you don't get an insurance policy on your character sheet. You don't get save states. You lose your daiklave...well, dice were rolled. Them's the breaks. Thievy McNightcaste is tearing towards Nexus right now to fence it for infinite hookers and blow...what are you going to do about it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:15:39-08:00","id":391655,"title":"","content":"Hmm, if orichalcum is the material with the &quot;best&quot; associations for demonic artifacts, it could serve to reinforce some of the Immaculate propaganda about the Anathema, even among the educated, and would help play up the Sol = Lucifer thing that is never directly addressed. (At least when it isn't Sol = Jesus and an Ishvara is Lucifer)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:20:49-08:00","id":391662,"title":"","content":"This thread is bringing up bad memories.<br /> <br /> I played in a Werewolf game where another player stole my klaive, a pretty big part of my character concept, and there was literally shit I could do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:30:25-08:00","id":391666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391477#post391477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that somebody had already posted up this quote in this thread:<br /> I am posting it here because some replies seem to be coming from a place that was unaware of it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, rereading the idea for how Stormcaller works, I wonder if &quot;sorcerous power&quot; might also entail Evocations that require on a need for certain conditions to build up in a manner akin to shaping actions for spells. Evocations in general (or at least Volcano Cutter) do seem to rely on a measure of preamble, from what they've been saying, but perhaps there would be a distinction between them.<br /> <br /> Still, if it's more about being like sorcery shaping than being like spells, it might be that things with an Infernal aspect would be more spread around. I mean, following my prior assumption, it wasn't that you'd get nothing for using Hellish magic to make a weapon from moonsilver or whatever, just less of an image of directly using the demonic magic and more the weapon doing what moonsilver does with a certain organic edge; not just being protean, but shaping itself into a big venomous maw or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orichalcum has more associations than just sorcerous power; none of the magical materials are that thematically narrow. Stormcaller expresses other aspects of orichalcum, as well as its own unique construction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:58:01-08:00","id":391709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391624#post391624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially if they lead to ideas like &quot;you can't use orichalcum to make something against the Unconquered Sun&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a thing people are actually suggesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:29:17-08:00","id":391749,"title":"","content":"It's also like, so damn dangerous to try and steal a daiklave from a solar dawn caste. If you fuck up that roll for larceny and stealth your head will be on the ground before you even realize you made a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T13:43:20-08:00","id":391801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391662#post391662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is bringing up bad memories.<br /> <br /> I played in a Werewolf game where another player stole my klaive, a pretty big part of my character concept, and there was literally shit I could do about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another player? I assume you no longer associate with them because they were clearly an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:03:02-08:00","id":391826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391801#post391801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another player? I assume you no longer associate with them because they were clearly an asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't deal with anyone in that group with one exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:35:43-08:00","id":391864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=389805#post389805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did specifically say &amp;quot;take away his weapon as part of a <b>plot</b>&amp;quot;. Losing your weapon because your an idiot is not a plot device. Nor is having an Abyssal cut your arm off (though losing an arm doesn't preclude you from using your off-hand to retrieve your weapon). As for dead, come on Jutlander, now you're just being silly.<br /> <br /> I will point out that 2E specifically mentioned that if a single PC in a group dies, you can award a commensurate amount of XP to them for character creation to maintain overall balance and &amp;quot;fun&amp;quot; within the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that one crucial word - plot - in your post and I misinterpreted your meaning about balancing. I was not intentionally silly; I was misguided. Oops, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:45:01-08:00","id":391875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391662#post391662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is bringing up bad memories.<br /> <br /> I played in a Werewolf game where another player stole my klaive, a pretty big part of my character concept, and there was literally shit I could do about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another player can straight-up kill you, and there's nothing you can buy to make sure that doesn't happen in any ST game, despite it being a much bigger deal than stealing someone's loot. So I don't think that's a problem that can be solved simply with plot armor for merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:54:01-08:00","id":391886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum has more associations than just sorcerous power; none of the magical materials are that thematically narrow. Stormcaller expresses other aspects of orichalcum</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not a wizard! <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a thing people are actually suggesting?</div> </div> </div> </div> TalosX is people, and the whole basis of dispute was &quot;because Unconquered Sun&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:20:52-08:00","id":391926,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda looking forward to all of sorcery, evocations, and martial arts, and if they interact. For instance, a character who is a sorcerer with a powerful magic staff, with evocations, and a staff based marital art. Probably not the strongest combatant, but certainly versatile. Mostly I'm curious to see how they work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/701-omniplex","name":"Omniplex","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:31:26-08:00","id":391942,"title":"","content":"I vaguely recall it being mentioned that you might start to feel spread a bit thin if you try to split your secondary XP amongst all 3 'outside your natural powers' avenues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:36:02-08:00","id":391951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391942#post391942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely recall it being mentioned that you might start to feel spread a bit thin if you try to split your secondary XP amongst all 3 'outside your natural powers' avenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, but I do wonder how much investment in any of those is practical, that is, if I could pick up, say, a single evocation on a weapon, and have that be meaningful in conjunction with other powers. Specialization is probably more useful anyway, I suppose I'll see when the book finally drops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/701-omniplex","name":"Omniplex","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T16:05:46-08:00","id":391989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omniplex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391951#post391951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense, but I do wonder how much investment in any of those is practical, that is, if I could pick up, say, a single evocation on a weapon, and have that be meaningful in conjunction with other powers. Specialization is probably more useful anyway, I suppose I'll see when the book finally drops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on the Evocation. Just like it'd depend on the particular Charm or Spell. <br /> <br /> I also bet that once you pop, you can't stop...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T17:49:06-08:00","id":392084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391886#post391886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TalosX is people, and the whole basis of dispute was &quot;because Unconquered Sun&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please enlighten me and point out where I said &quot;you can't use orichalcum to make something against the Unconquered Sun&quot;? It would be much appreciated, since I never said it. What I said was while orichalcum could be used in demon themes, I do not believe it is the PREFERRED material. I actually said it in multiple posts.<br /> <br /> If you disagree, that's fine. Don't try and call me out on things I've never said though. I referenced several facts that UCS and orichalcum have strong links to one another. Not once did I say orichalcum couldn't be used against the Unconquered Sun. I could also point out that moonsilver and Luna have strong links, but you might misconstrue that as me saying &quot;Only Lunars can use moonsilver and moonsilver weapons can't hurt Luna!&quot; <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T23:10:48-08:00","id":392390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391942#post391942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely recall it being mentioned that you might start to feel spread a bit thin if you try to split your secondary XP amongst all 3 'outside your natural powers' avenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know that Solar charms reward dabbling. Grabbing level 1 charms will give you cool toys to play with while level 2 ones will be more focused and powerful.<br /> <br /> I imagine that if you want to play the guy who can shoot 9 suns out of the sky, you'd want to invest heavily in archery charms as well as go deep into the evocation tree for your bow. You might still dabble in Emerald level sorcery (just grabbing demon summoning makes that worthwhile) and a martial art that helps you deal with the times you're forced to fight in melee range.<br /> <br /> I assume you only feel spread thin if you're attempting to become good at all three, as opposed to great with one and rounding out your character with low-level powers/abilities from anothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T23:58:37-08:00","id":392419,"title":"","content":"All of the above, my friend. All of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T00:03:18-08:00","id":392421,"title":"","content":"All i know is that:<br /> <br /> Sorcery + martial prowess + evocations =<br /> <br /> ELRIC!<br /> <br /> Summon an elemental to aid you in battle, then fight alongside that elemental with your martial arts while using your evocations to smite your enemies.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying just doesnt get any better than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T05:44:43-08:00","id":392525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=392390#post392390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know that Solar charms reward dabbling. Grabbing level 1 charms will give you cool toys to play with while level 2 ones will be more focused and powerful.<br /> <br /> I imagine that if you want to play the guy who can shoot 9 suns out of the sky, you'd want to invest heavily in archery charms as well as go deep into the evocation tree for your bow. You might still dabble in Emerald level sorcery (just grabbing demon summoning makes that worthwhile) and a martial art that helps you deal with the times you're forced to fight in melee range.<br /> <br /> I assume you only feel spread thin if you're attempting to become good at all three, as opposed to great with one and rounding out your character with low-level powers/abilities from anothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also with free excellencies and stuff we're going to have a lot more charms to play with anyway, way easier to take a little of everything that you want to do. If you wanted, it won't be &quot;optimal&quot; but you could use a lot of your regular xp to get evocations and stuff and really invest in being a Kung-fu artifact wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:21:43-08:00","id":393129,"title":"","content":"It'll be years, before I ever sit down and play a game of Ex3, with my current group, assuming I don't just run it myself. Even today, Holden's question back in that MoJ thread has me hopeful.<br /> <br /> If I do manage to get in another group, think I'll go with my usual comfort zones of sneaking, hiding, ranged combat, that kind of thing. Then again, Evocations has interested me since I first heard about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:27:37-08:00","id":393134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=392390#post392390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that if you want to play the guy who can shoot 9 suns out of the sky, you'd want to invest heavily in archery charms as well as go deep into the evocation tree for your bow. You might still dabble in Emerald level sorcery (just grabbing demon summoning makes that worthwhile) and a martial art that helps you deal with the times you're forced to fight in melee range.<br /> <br /> I assume you only feel spread thin if you're attempting to become good at all three, as opposed to great with one and rounding out your character with low-level powers/abilities from anothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think sorcery will be the easiest to dabble in, given that Spells are stand-alone effects, while both MA and Evocations exist in trees. Trees provide an incentive to get to the end of the tree for internal effect synergy, after all - and as was said, Wood Dragon's Claw or Evocations on in-form Artifact weapons can probably improve most all Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T05:05:33-08:00","id":394690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=391666#post391666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum has more associations than just sorcerous power; none of the magical materials are that thematically narrow. Stormcaller expresses other aspects of orichalcum, as well as its own unique construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orichalcum is pure, distilled, badassitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:02:39-08:00","id":394712,"title":"","content":"Probably sorcery, because I play a sorcerer. I am interested to see better balanced CMA, but seeing better-written versions of styles I know, while very important, isnt' that exciting. Evocations might be interesting, but sorcery is the only one I'm really intrigued by. How do these different initiations work? I heard you can get sorcery by making pacts with demons and it actually makes a difference to how it works, that sounds excellent. Then there's Wyld initiation, and 3 others (I think they said there's 5). And then there's these rituals to gather the motes. Is that part of the initiations? Or separate?<br /> And now I'll apparently be able to do all these different interesting magic rituals (are they free? Do you buy them like spells? I assume not or they'd just be spells. Maybe you pay XP each time you use them?) that I couldn't before. Sounds excellent. It might make me buy Celestial Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Possibly of course, were I playing a martial artist, or a guy who owned a magic weapon (my artefacts are a spellbook that I can only read on the new moon, and orichalcum lamellar, ie the wrong magic material for a Lunar), I might be more excited by them instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T20:02:09-08:00","id":395779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=392390#post392390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know that Solar charms reward dabbling. Grabbing level 1 charms will give you cool toys to play with while level 2 ones will be more focused and powerful.<br /> <br /> I imagine that if you want to play the guy who can shoot 9 suns out of the sky, you'd want to invest heavily in archery charms as well as go deep into the evocation tree for your bow. You might still dabble in Emerald level sorcery (just grabbing demon summoning makes that worthwhile) and a martial art that helps you deal with the times you're forced to fight in melee range.<br /> <br /> I assume you only feel spread thin if you're attempting to become good at all three, as opposed to great with one and rounding out your character with low-level powers/abilities from anothers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can definitely climb the Solar Archery tree and raise the Evocations on your powerbow at the same time. Try to add in a martial art or grab a bunch of spells and yes it will slow down. It's worth noting here that I wrote the Solar Charm set with it specifically in mind that you would never be able to buy everything. Even in a single Ability tree it is unlikely you will be able to buy everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T20:15:55-08:00","id":395780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395779#post395779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can definitely climb the Solar Archery tree and raise the Evocations on your powerbow at the same time. Try to add in a martial art or grab a bunch of spells and yes it will slow down. It's worth noting here that I wrote the Solar Charm set with it specifically in mind that you would never be able to buy everything. Even in a single Ability tree it is unlikely you will be able to buy everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it that you wont be able to <b>afford</b> taking the entire tree, or that a tree goes in enough niche directions that you probably won't<b> need</b> to take it all?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T20:24:40-08:00","id":395787,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine it is a diminishing returns sort of thing where you are better off spreading out into other abilities instead of trying to buy every charm in a single tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T20:36:02-08:00","id":395800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395787#post395787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine it is a diminishing returns sort of thing where you are better off spreading out into other abilities instead of trying to buy every charm in a single tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I am hoping the new charm trees avoid is that situation where you want a pinnacle charm at the end of the tree, and there are two branches that you need leading to it...but only one of them really feels connected to the pinnacle charm, the other branch is either just different enough from the pinnacle that there is no guarantee a character even wants it, or blatantly situational speed-bump charms that you may never use. Solar Resistance and DB Thrown are what immediately come to mind as cases where I was buying charms that I didn't want just to get the pinnacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T21:06:16-08:00","id":395810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395779#post395779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can definitely climb the Solar Archery tree and raise the Evocations on your powerbow at the same time. Try to add in a martial art or grab a bunch of spells and yes it will slow down. It's worth noting here that I wrote the Solar Charm set with it specifically in mind that you would never be able to buy everything. Even in a single Ability tree it is unlikely you will be able to buy everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am now morbidly curious how things would be affected if a GM just said &quot;Okay, high powered game, 10,000 XP for everyone, go nuts!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T22:09:14-08:00","id":395839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395810#post395810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now morbidly curious how things would be affected if a GM just said &quot;Okay, high powered game, 10,000 XP for everyone, go nuts!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Having joined long-running games where I had to spend literally 1000+ XP at chargen, it would suck and be awful. <br /> <br /> If you want to do a super high-XP start, I'd take the alternate rules for experienced character chargen that will be in the corebook, and then ramp them up to the Nth degree instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T23:36:51-08:00","id":395876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395779#post395779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can definitely climb the Solar Archery tree and raise the Evocations on your powerbow at the same time. Try to add in a martial art or grab a bunch of spells and yes it will slow down. It's worth noting here that I wrote the Solar Charm set with it specifically in mind that you would never be able to buy everything. Even in a single Ability tree it is unlikely you will be able to buy everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>....challenge....accepted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T00:00:53-08:00","id":395900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395779#post395779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Even in a single Ability tree it is unlikely you will be able to buy everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow.<br /> <br /> /6char","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T00:04:31-08:00","id":395902,"title":"","content":"I am ok with the statement that you're not going to be able to buy everything. While I am a competitionist when it comes to video game rpgs it just never hit me with Exalted. I think this is in part because I tend to approach a character in Exalted as an actor in a play and I want a niche, and usually that niche does not involve KNOW ALL THE THINGS! though I can see that angle for some characters. Evocations, while not as enticing to me as Martial Arts are I think is an awesome bridge mechanic because it, imho, adds both mythic elements to the artifact itself but to the sort of combat mythos you want to build in the game world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:50:06-08:00","id":396046,"title":"","content":"I am also a completionist with rpgs, but the point is that you get everything by the end of the game. And pen-and-paper RPGs don't tend to end the same way. So I might think &quot;I want this character to be an awesome swordsman who will get better and better at being a swordsman&quot; but I don't actually want to be able to buy all the Melee charms because, well, what will I buy then? How will he get better at being a swordsman? Being the world's greatest swordsman may be his goal, but once he's achieved that the character's less interesting. It's the development and struggle to become the world's greatest swordsman.<br /> One thing I disliked about 2nd ed is that with a lot of the charm trees, you could very quickly get everything in them (especially the Night caste charm trees) and then there was no more room to develop that part of your character.<br /> So this makes me pleased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T03:34:04-08:00","id":396069,"title":"","content":"I am most exited about evocations, they feel right at home in exalted, though new sorcery is intriuging as well, but when reading these pages a question poped up in my mind.<br /> <br /> What will happen to Glorious Solar Saber and the like in 3e.<br /> Are they gonna be obselete? or do we able to create evocations for &quot;our&quot; glorious solar grimaxe, and channel them after summoning it?<br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T03:51:16-08:00","id":396100,"title":"","content":"I get the idea that, with Charms representing the kind of hero you are, each tree is home to several archetypes within that ability. Like, you might want to be &quot;the best captain at sea&quot; without necessarily being &quot;the fastest boat pilot&quot;<br /> <br /> So, not only you might not be able to get all the dozens of published Charms for a given Ability (especially since you likely want at least a few Charms in other Abilities too) but you might not <i>want</i> all the Charms in there, simply because not all of them are appropriate building blocks for your concept. This edition is supposed to very encouraging of homebrew, after all, so even if you get tons of XP over time to expend on Charms, you might want to have custom Charms that go well with you concept, instead of having your ultimate strongman become also a runner because you got all the strongman Charms already.<br /> <br /> This allows a circle to have, say, 4 people focusing on melee, yet having different playstyles and feel in combat.You could have one fencing with a rapier, another dual-wielding axes, another with a sword and shied, and a another with a huge two-handed hammer. And they could be different in play via multiple things - different stats and tags on their weapons, different Evocations, <i>and</i> different selections of melee Charms, resulting in 4 characters with quite distinct approaches to combat, despite all going deep into melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T04:16:24-08:00","id":396105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396069#post396069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am most exited about evocations, they feel right at home in exalted, though new sorcery is intriuging as well, but when reading these pages a question poped up in my mind.<br /> <br /> What will happen to Glorious Solar Saber and the like in 3e.<br /> Are they gonna be obselete? or do we able to create evocations for &quot;our&quot; glorious solar grimaxe, and channel them after summoning it?<br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I reckon the second one. That would be most likely.<br /> <br /> Danelsan, I like that idea, you should be able to have a swordsman and a with a tetsubo and not have them feel like they're basically the same (except Tetsubo guy is better because he does more damage, of course) and 2nd ed was a bit like that. You generally just had to use completely different charm trees.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:10:29-08:00","id":396307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395839#post395839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to do a super high-XP start, I'd take the alternate rules for experienced character chargen that will be in the corebook, and then ramp them up to the Nth degree instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>we are going to have proper rules for creating experienced character!!!!<br /> no that thing were if you have 600 years the you have 1,000+ 750 + ([100 \u2013 25] x 10)=2500 experience points<br /> im crying bloody tears of happiness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:12:32-08:00","id":396310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396069#post396069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am most exited about evocations, they feel right at home in exalted, though new sorcery is intriuging as well, but when reading these pages a question poped up in my mind.<br /> <br /> What will happen to Glorious Solar Saber and the like in 3e.<br /> Are they gonna be obselete? or do we able to create evocations for &quot;our&quot; glorious solar grimaxe, and channel them after summoning it?<br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Devs have already stated that Glorious Solar Saber exists, but does not have Evocations. That makes sense since you can form a bond with a weapon you create with your own essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:19:48-08:00","id":396325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395780#post395780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it that you wont be able to <b>afford</b> taking the entire tree, or that a tree goes in enough niche directions that you probably won't<b> need</b> to take it all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it means that while you can purchase every published Archery Charm (or whatever), (1) you can't at chargen, even if you meet all prereqs because there are just too damn many Charms; (2) there will be diminishing returns; and (3) if you set out to do so, you will also be mono-focused to a degree that it might very well be pointless to do so (classic situation of a Killfuck Soulshitter with nothing to do in social scenes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395839#post395839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having joined long-running games where I had to spend literally 1000+ XP at chargen, it would suck and be awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It really turns chargen into a crippling and exhausting slog. And then you have a bunch of shit on your character sheet that you don't necessarily know how it all works together, because the growth was not very organic and there's no play experience to rely on.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396069#post396069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they gonna be obselete? or do we able to create evocations for &quot;our&quot; glorious solar grimaxe, and channel them after summoning it?<br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not assume that &quot;can't make Evocations for this&quot; means my light-forged soul-sword is obsolete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:26:28-08:00","id":396335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396325#post396325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. It really turns chargen into a crippling and exhausting slog. And then you have a bunch of shit on your character sheet that you don't necessarily know how it all works together, because the growth was not very organic and there's no play experience to rely on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, you pretty much always forget something important which, if you'd grown organically, you'd have forgotten.<br /> People tend to make much more specialised characters as well, because they haven't had to deal with a wide variety of situations in play which caused them to buy stuff outside their favoured abilities.<br /> (In pretty much every long-running Exalted game I've run or played, most people end up with Linguistics 5 for example)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:14:27-08:00","id":396409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396335#post396335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you pretty much always forget something important which, if you'd grown organically, you'd have forgotten.<br /> People tend to make much more specialised characters as well, because they haven't had to deal with a wide variety of situations in play which caused them to buy stuff outside their favoured abilities.<br /> (In pretty much every long-running Exalted game I've run or played, most people end up with Linguistics 5 for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's funny because I have always really liked having a ton of XP to spend, you can buy WAY into a tree so you are an expert in it, and still have lots of XP left over to buy other charms that support your characters concept (even if they are few charms into some other tree), and boost up your abilities and attributes. My large point buy characters have tended to be my most balanced characters with charms from the widest selection of trees. I can see the benefit of organically making a character, but if you think back to the things your past characters have needed you can probably fill most of those gaps for the new character. Think, do I need; Ghost-Eating, Essence Vision, Surprise Negation, Environmental Protection, Shaping Defenses, Movement Charms, all those things you have decided to pick up in the past after finding yourself stuck without them in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:16:00-08:00","id":396410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396335#post396335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you pretty much always forget something important which, if you'd grown organically, you'd have forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396335#post396335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In pretty much every long-running Exalted game I've run or played, most people end up with Linguistics 5 for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this just for languages? If so, I'm glad that's changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:15:35-08:00","id":396465,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just for languages. We had to make a house rule of how to buy more languages after 6 (base+5 linguistics) for the high-XP DB game.<br /> After all, as a DB scholar you're going to have High, Low and Old Realm and Riverspeak, stick on 4 directional languages and you've got 2 more than the rules let you learn. Now, saying you can't get more than 5 dots in melee plus 3 specialities I can understand, but learning more than 6 languages is something mortal men can do.<br /> There was also the way that Languages were just either something you couldn't do at all, or were something you were fluent in. I hope that they're perhaps 1 or 2 dot merits: ie you can buy 1 dot to speak some basic phrases, 2 dots to speak it fluently. Something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:24:38-08:00","id":396473,"title":"","content":"I have a sneaking suspicion that one of the differences between this edition and second edition in regards to why there are so many charms has to do with developing characters organically. As weird as it sounds I imagine writing Charms under the idea that they are representations of what your character does(internal) vs what your character can do(external) means you're already tapping into a hell of a lot more narrative space to play with mechanically. That in and of itself potentially leads you to simply not exploring any given charm tree of an Ability because the focus wont be on make sure I have mechanical effect X,Y,Z available in my Charm list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:59:27-08:00","id":396516,"title":"","content":"Re: GSS, yes, from &quot;what we know&quot; &lt;i&gt;&quot;Q: Will essence-created artifact weapons and armor, like Glorious Solar Saber or Refining the Inner Blade, include their own Evocations? (Sparda219) A: Doubtful. (Holden)&quot;&lt;/i&gt;<br /> <br /> I'm sure I remembered some specific commentary in one of the Developer questions threads about Glorious Solar Saber, but can't find it, so perhaps its a figment.<br /> <br /> There might be ways to build on GSS which don't operate through Evocation mechanics - possible certain GSS building Charms which are nonetheless Solar XP OK?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:06:53-08:00","id":396525,"title":"","content":"I think it was mentioned somewhere in the RPG.Net threads that Evocations are part of GSS' customization somehow? I would guess that GSS allows Solars to use Evocations without their Artifact weapon even if they normally wouldn't be able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:35:24-08:00","id":396549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396465#post396465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just for languages. We had to make a house rule of how to buy more languages after 6 (base+5 linguistics) for the high-XP DB game.<br /> After all, as a DB scholar you're going to have High, Low and Old Realm and Riverspeak, stick on 4 directional languages and you've got 2 more than the rules let you learn. Now, saying you can't get more than 5 dots in melee plus 3 specialities I can understand, but learning more than 6 languages is something mortal men can do.<br /> There was also the way that Languages were just either something you couldn't do at all, or were something you were fluent in. I hope that they're perhaps 1 or 2 dot merits: ie you can buy 1 dot to speak some basic phrases, 2 dots to speak it fluently. Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been confirmed that languages known will be handled by merits now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:42:04-08:00","id":396560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396516#post396516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: GSS, yes, from &quot;what we know&quot; &lt;i&gt;&quot;Q: Will essence-created artifact weapons and armor, like Glorious Solar Saber or Refining the Inner Blade, include their own Evocations? (Sparda219) A: Doubtful. (Holden)&quot;&lt;/i&gt;<br /> <br /> I'm sure I remembered some specific commentary in one of the Developer questions threads about Glorious Solar Saber, but can't find it, so perhaps its a figment.<br /> <br /> There might be ways to build on GSS which don't operate through Evocation mechanics - possible certain GSS building Charms which are nonetheless Solar XP OK?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396525#post396525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was mentioned somewhere in the RPG.Net threads that Evocations are part of GSS' customization somehow? I would guess that GSS allows Solars to use Evocations without their Artifact weapon even if they normally wouldn't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm growing frustrated since I <i>know</i> I remember something like this, too. I don't think <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/01/27/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-post-6/\" target=\"_blank\">Minton's awesome summation</a> has quite caught up to it yet. The comment was something about how the Solar Charmset was designed in a certain fashion, in considering Evocations, but that GSS was the/an exception. Just... cannot recall the particulars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:50:05-08:00","id":396564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=395839#post395839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having joined long-running games where I had to spend literally 1000+ XP at chargen, it would suck and be awful.<br /> <br /> If you want to do a super high-XP start, I'd take the alternate rules for experienced character chargen that will be in the corebook, and then ramp them up to the Nth degree instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396335#post396335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you pretty much always forget something important which, if you'd grown organically, you'd have forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> <br /> Based on that, if I was given a ton of XP to build a starting character, I guess it would be safe to choose much less than twice as many Charms or Merits as a 0xp character would have, and sink everything else into passive traits like Attributes, Abilities, and Specialties.<br /> <br /> The character would lack &quot;burst excellence&quot;, but would still be pretty potent before using Charms. Would also have less need to spend Peripheral Essence.<br /> <br /> This also frees me up to spend any further XP on Charms and Merits, since I've already got all of the Ability or Attribute minimums met for anything I would want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T14:08:53-08:00","id":396767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=396564#post396564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> Based on that, if I was given a ton of XP to build a starting character, I guess it would be safe to choose much less than twice as many Charms or Merits as a 0xp character would have, and sink everything else into passive traits like Attributes, Abilities, and Specialties.<br /> <br /> The character would lack &quot;burst excellence&quot;, but would still be pretty potent before using Charms. Would also have less need to spend Peripheral Essence.<br /> <br /> This also frees me up to spend any further XP on Charms and Merits, since I've already got all of the Ability or Attribute minimums met for anything I would want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found it pretty easy to spend lots of XP, Attributes and abilities would eat up the majority of it quickly. Charms fitting to concept take up a good deal of what is left.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just because I identify an ideal end state as how I want my character to develop as part of the character Creation Process, with a great big wishlist of stuff I want the character to get. With that I can just start checking stuff off the list when I have the XP to burn.<br /> <br /> 1000 XP goes pretty fast if you already know what you want an advanced character to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T18:00:49-08:00","id":397017,"title":"","content":"Evocations, though the the limitation they'll have when it comes to evocations for magitech has me a little down. I was thinking of a character while not going full alchemical transhumanism route I wanted to show a synchronization with an implant increasing via an evocation tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T18:12:02-08:00","id":397030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/386678-solars-what-foreign-magic-are-you-most-excited-for?p=397017#post397017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations, though the the limitation they'll have when it comes to evocations for magitech has me a little down. I was thinking of a character while not going full alchemical transhumanism route I wanted to show a synchronization with an implant increasing via an evocation tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can probably still make that. Sidereal Canon Police Ninja Death squads have pretty glass cannon battle group stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}